{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Activation Functions Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Implement All Activation Functions with Derivatives"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each function takes a single float and returns a float. Each derivative function takes the same input and returns the gradient."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = max(-500, min(500, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid_derivative(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = sigmoid(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return s * (1 - s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tanh_act(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return math.tanh(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tanh_derivative(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = math.tanh(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1 - t * t"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def relu(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return max(0.0, x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def relu_derivative(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 if x > 0 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def leaky_relu(x, alpha=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x if x > 0 else alpha * x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def leaky_relu_derivative(x, alpha=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 if x > 0 else alpha"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gelu(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 0.5 * x * (1 + math.tanh(math.sqrt(2 / math.pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x ** 3)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gelu_derivative(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    phi = 0.5 * (1 + math.erf(x / math.sqrt(2)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pdf = math.exp(-0.5 * x * x) / math.sqrt(2 * math.pi)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return phi + x * pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def swish(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x * sigmoid(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def swish_derivative(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = sigmoid(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return s + x * s * (1 - s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(xs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_x = max(xs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exps = [math.exp(x - max_x) for x in xs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = sum(exps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [e / total for e in exps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Visualize Where Gradients Die"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compute the gradient at 100 evenly-spaced points from -5 to 5. Print a text histogram showing where each activation's gradient is near-zero."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gradient_scan(name, derivative_fn, start=-5, end=5, n=100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    step = (end - start) / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    near_zero = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    healthy = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = start + i * step"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        g = derivative_fn(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if abs(g) < 0.01:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            near_zero += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            healthy += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pct_dead = near_zero / n * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{name:15s}: {healthy:3d} healthy, {near_zero:3d} near-zero ({pct_dead:.0f}% dead zone)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gradient_scan(\"Sigmoid\", sigmoid_derivative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gradient_scan(\"Tanh\", tanh_derivative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gradient_scan(\"ReLU\", relu_derivative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gradient_scan(\"Leaky ReLU\", leaky_relu_derivative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gradient_scan(\"GELU\", gelu_derivative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gradient_scan(\"Swish\", swish_derivative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Vanishing Gradient Experiment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Forward-pass a signal through N layers using sigmoid vs ReLU. Measure how the activation magnitude changes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def vanishing_gradient_experiment(activation_fn, name, n_layers=10, n_inputs=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    values = [random.gauss(0, 1) for _ in range(n_inputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\n{name} through {n_layers} layers:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for layer in range(n_layers):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        weights = [random.gauss(0, 1) for _ in range(n_inputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        z = sum(w * v for w, v in zip(weights, values))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        activated = activation_fn(z)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        magnitude = abs(activated)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        bar = \"#\" * int(magnitude * 20)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Layer {layer+1:2d}: magnitude = {magnitude:.6f} {bar}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        values = [activated] * n_inputs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vanishing_gradient_experiment(sigmoid, \"Sigmoid\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vanishing_gradient_experiment(relu, \"ReLU\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vanishing_gradient_experiment(gelu, \"GELU\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Dead Neuron Detector"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Create a ReLU network, pass random inputs through it, count how many neurons never fire."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def dead_neuron_detector(n_inputs=5, hidden_size=20, n_samples=1000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weights = [[random.gauss(0, 1) for _ in range(n_inputs)] for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    biases = [random.gauss(0, 1) for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fire_counts = [0] * hidden_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n_samples):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        inputs = [random.gauss(0, 1) for _ in range(n_inputs)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for neuron_idx in range(hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            z = sum(w * x for w, x in zip(weights[neuron_idx], inputs)) + biases[neuron_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if relu(z) > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                fire_counts[neuron_idx] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dead = sum(1 for c in fire_counts if c == 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rarely_fire = sum(1 for c in fire_counts if 0 < c < n_samples * 0.05)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    healthy = hidden_size - dead - rarely_fire"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\nDead Neuron Report ({hidden_size} neurons, {n_samples} samples):\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Dead (never fired):     {dead}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Barely alive (<5%):     {rarely_fire}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Healthy:                {healthy}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Dead neuron rate:       {dead/hidden_size*100:.1f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, c in enumerate(fire_counts):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        status = \"DEAD\" if c == 0 else \"WEAK\" if c < n_samples * 0.05 else \"OK\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        bar = \"#\" * (c * 40 // n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Neuron {i:2d}: {c:4d}/{n_samples} fires [{status:4s}] {bar}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dead_neuron_detector()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Training Comparison -- Sigmoid vs ReLU vs GELU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Train the same two-layer network on the circle dataset (points inside a circle = class 1, outside = class 0) with three different activations. Compare convergence speed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_circle_data(n=200, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    random.seed(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    data = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = random.uniform(-2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        label = 1.0 if x * x + y * y < 1.5 else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        data.append(([x, y], label))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ActivationNetwork:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, activation_fn, activation_deriv, hidden_size=8, lr=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        random.seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.act = activation_fn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.act_d = activation_deriv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = lr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.hidden_size = hidden_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w1 = [[random.gauss(0, 0.5) for _ in range(2)] for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b1 = [0.0] * hidden_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w2 = [random.gauss(0, 0.5) for _ in range(hidden_size)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b2 = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.x = x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.z1 = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.h = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            z = self.w1[i][0] * x[0] + self.w1[i][1] * x[1] + self.b1[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.z1.append(z)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.h.append(self.act(z))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.z2 = sum(self.w2[i] * self.h[i] for i in range(self.hidden_size)) + self.b2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.out = sigmoid(self.z2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def backward(self, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        error = self.out - target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        d_out = error * self.out * (1 - self.out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(self.hidden_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            d_h = d_out * self.w2[i] * self.act_d(self.z1[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.w2[i] -= self.lr * d_out * self.h[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.w1[i][j] -= self.lr * d_h * self.x[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.b1[i] -= self.lr * d_h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b2 -= self.lr * d_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self, data, epochs=200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_loss = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for x, y in data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pred = self.forward(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.backward(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                total_loss += (pred - y) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if (pred >= 0.5) == (y >= 0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            avg_loss = total_loss / len(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            accuracy = correct / len(data) * 100"
